   Okay, I agree that formally, I do need a tu'a for a djica 2 (although I
have always argued against that, although this is neither here nor there).
 And yes, I have always thought that we should have a "choose from list"
cmavo, for cases of >2 choices.  I was just wondering why in the particular
case being bandied about, the "?"connectors weren't being mentioned.

          --gejyspa



